docs/lab.ko.md says when to use each.

  ./lab start PROJECT_ID     step 1: tools, GitHub sign-in, APIs, image registry, the first images
  ./lab base                 step 3: expiry rules, index, bucket, service accounts, secrets
  ./lab iam                  step 3: who may do what, by service account
  ./lab env [web|job|github] values to paste into the Console and GitHub
  ./lab workers              step 6: ticket-worker, waitlist-promoter, mailer and their grants
  ./lab code                 your latest sign-in code, from the logs
  ./lab warmup               step 13: pre-warming's custom role and act-as
  ./lab deployer             step 15: the deployer's three roles
  ./lab check [STEP ...]     check what you built (every step so far without STEP)
  ./lab check --report       every step, saved to ~/lab-report.txt for submission
  ./lab skip STEP            build a hand step for you; the report shows it as skipped
  ./lab pause                step 26: pause the Scheduler, turn off deploys
  ./lab down                 delete everything the lab made in Google Cloud

Shortcuts build their part with Terraform (infra/lab.tf). Each creates only what is
